# Factor generation in 15.3.49(i)–(j)

Preparation transports the selected quadratic best offender by H-conjugation.
ClassificationPreparation establishes all B.5.3 hypotheses on the actual
restricted section action, including its explicit SQTK quotient presentation.
Theta lifts the order-three generators through the two-core quotient.
StarLifting transports relative normalization and commutator containment.
SolvableFactor derives the intrinsic S₃ quotient, normalization by Y₀, and
escaping cubic generators for a candidate from the B.5.6 analysis.

Still required are the geometric placement of the selected conjugate, the
exhaustive B.5.6 factor analysis and perfect lifting, and the rank-two module
contradiction. In particular this module does not yet assert (i) or (j).
Their final assembly remains with this task.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), printed
pp.1143–1144, using B.5.3 and B.5.6 on pp.104–110.
